<article class="env-lemma" id="085Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/085Z">Lemma <span data-tag="085Z">71.17.11</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}_ X$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. Let $b : X' \to X$ be the blowing up of $X$ in the ideal sheaf $\mathcal{I}$. If $\mathcal{I}$ is of finite type, then $b : X' \to X$ is a proper morphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U$ be a scheme and let $U \to X$ be a surjective étale morphism. As blowing up commutes with flat base change (Lemma <a href="/tag/085S" data-tag="085S">71.17.3</a>) we can prove each of these statements after base change to $U$ (see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/083R" data-tag="083R">67.40.2</a>). This reduces us to the case of schemes. In this case the morphism $b$ is projective by Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/02NS" data-tag="02NS">31.33.13</a> hence proper by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01WC" data-tag="01WC">29.44.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>